# What prettier must not touch when run from the REPO ROOT.
#
# Note how prettier resolves this: unlike the config (resolved per file, walking up), the
# ignore file is read relative to the working directory. So this file governs a root-level
# `prettier --write .`, while a workspace's own `.prettierignore` governs `npm run
# format:check -w <workspace>`. Both need the load-bearing entries below — a rule that lives
# in only one of them holds for only one of the two ways we invoke prettier.

# These use gitignore syntax: a pattern with no slash matches at ANY depth, so `dist/` already
# covers every workspace's dist and needs no `**/` prefix.
node_modules/
dist/
.make/
.nuxt/
.output/
.data/
.nitro/

package-lock.json
extension/public/

# Same shape, surfaced once Markdown came into scope (#737): www-docs/content/ is assembled
# from /docs and the app booklets by build-content.mjs on every docs build. CI's Formatting
# job never sees it (fresh checkout, no docs build), but anyone who has built the docs does —
# and without this, `npm run format` rewrites generated Markdown and format:check fails
# locally while passing in CI. Format the SOURCE under /docs, which this sweep did.
www-docs/content/

# Same shape again (#748): VitePress writes its Vite dependency pre-bundle cache to
# .vitepress/cache/ (`npm run dev`/`build` -w @kimtos/www-docs, ~15 files under cache/deps/,
# e.g. vue.js, dayjs.js). It's gitignored (www-docs/.gitignore) but that does not help —
# prettier never reads .gitignore. CI never sees it (fresh checkout, no docs build), but
# anyone who has built or run the docs locally does, and format:check fails on generated
# dependency bundles that are not ours to format. www-docs/dist/ (the VitePress build output)
# needs no entry of its own — the `dist/` pattern above already matches it at any depth.
www-docs/.vitepress/cache/

# LOAD-BEARING: prompt Markdown is literal model input, not prose. Prettier rewrites `>>>`
# (a delimiter the parser depends on) into `> > >` (a blockquote) and the prompt stops
# working. This is why shared-modules/prompts carries its own .prettierignore; the same rule
# has to exist here or a root-level sweep destroys what that file protects.
shared-modules/prompts/prompts/
shared-modules/prompts/src/generated.ts

# CLAUDE.md is formatted like every other Markdown file — NOT excluded. It briefly was (#742):
# prettier would not CONVERGE on it, re-indenting the continuation paragraphs in the checklist
# under "Before the first public / commercial release" by four more spaces every pass (10 -> 14
# -> 18). #741 fixed that at the source by restructuring the one offending item, so the file now
# reaches a fixed point and is swept with the rest. If it ever fails `format:check` on that block
# again, restructure the item — do not re-add an exclusion here.

# One thing to leave alone if you touch .prettierrc.json: `proseWrap` must stay at its default
# of `preserve`. Setting it to `always` rewraps every paragraph, and scripts/check-agent-claims
# .mjs matches capability claims line by line — rewrapping silently changes what it catches.

# NOT ignored, deliberately: www/data/apps.ts is generated
# and committed, but its generator call prettier's own resolveConfig + format before
# writing (#559), so its output already matches whatever this config says. Checking them is
# therefore free and catches the generator drifting from the repo style — which is the exact
# bug #559 fixed. Ignoring them would re-open it.
